Package: gdam
Title: Fast robust additive models using gamma divergence
Version: 0.1
Date: 2025-02-28
Authors@R: c(
    person("Francis KC", "Hui", , "fhui28@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0765-3533"))
           )
Description: gdam is designed to be computationally fast (at least at the time of development!) method of robust additive modeling based on the gamma divergence. The package works by assuming an identity link function and a normal distribution for the errors, and then adapting the gamma divergence to the resulting restricted maximum likelihood function (REML) to produce a new loss function (hence the name gdam, which stands for gamma divergence additive models) that is design to be most robust to outlying observations. gdam takes a `gam` fit from the `mgcv` package as a starting point for optimization of the gamma divergence, and so as a result can exploit many/some of the smoothing options available in the `mgcv` package for additive models.
